A thread that waits ends its share's turn even though another thread of the share is ready.
The share would drop off the run queue with that thread on its ring and never have a turn again;
every share with a ready thread but the one whose turn it is waits on the run queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a share with a ready thread is not on the run queue

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -392,9 +392,7 @@ static void run_turn(void)
 void sched_run_next(void)
 {
     /* The share whose turn it is keeps it while it has another thread ready. */
-    if (turn == NULL || turn->threads == 0) {
-        turn = next_turn();
-    }
+    turn = next_turn();
     run_turn();
 }
 
